04-15","finding":"Documented Annual Training - 1 hour in Prevention, Recognition and Reporting of child maltreatment: One out of eight employee records evaluated were lacking one hour of training in child maltreatment for the most recent completed training year.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026380574","violation_type_title":"Documented Annual Training - 1 hour in Prevention, Recognition and Reporting of child maltreatment (26 TAC §746.1309(c))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260407-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-613-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260407","date":"2026-04-07","original_code":"746.613(b)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-05-05","finding":"Immunization Records, Exceptions, and Exemptions Current: Three out of ten children records evaluated were lacking up to date immunization records on file.","topic":"health","source_record_id":"1026380575","violation_type_title":"Immunization Records, Exceptions, and Exemptions Current (26 TAC §746.613(b))","topic_label":"Health records & medication"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260407-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1315-b","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260407","date":"2026-04-07","original_code":"746.1315(b)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-04-28","finding":"Each Caregiver and the Director Must Have Current Training in pediatric CPR: Two caregivers did not have training in pediatric CPR prior to being unsupervised with children in the classroom. They were the only caregiver present in their respective buildings.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026299817","violation_type_title":"Each Caregiver and the Director Must Have Current Training in pediatric CPR (26 TAC §746.1315(b))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260406","date":"2026-04-06","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":3,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905917972","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905917972","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2026-04-06","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260406-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260406","date":"2026-04-06","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-05-11","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: Children were redirected inappropriately by two different caregivers during at least two separate incidents. A child was also left alone on the playground for a few seconds before another caregiver stepped in. The operation did not notify the parents of any of these incidents yet felt strongly enough to reprimand or address the issues with the caregivers. This demonstrates a pattern for a lack of good judgement.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026588787","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260406-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2805-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-369515-i20260406","date":"2026-04-06","original_code":"746.2805(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-05-11","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - Corporal Punishment: In two separate incidents, two different caregivers threatened corporal punishment to redirect children.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026588786","violation_type_